Code for this lesson is in the testOne.spec.ts file

Hooks let us save time setting up the environment before each test:
test.beforeEach(async({page}) => {
    code that is to be performed before each test.
    })

Another useful hook is 
test.beforeAll()
It performs code just once before any other test in the spec file is executed.

their opposites are:
test.afterEach()
test.afterAll()

It is good practice to user afterAll rather than afterEach, as if the latter causes any probles, all subsequent
tests will fail.